# 1. Run GET /auth/codeforces/login by opening it IN A BROWSER (not REST Client).
# 2. Sign in to Codeforces and approve the OAuth app.
# 3. After backend callback sets HttpOnly say_session cookie, copy its value
#    from browser developer tools (Application -> Cookies -> localhost).
# 4. Paste cookie only into a private .vscode/*.local.http copy of this file.
#    NEVER commit the real cookie/token.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001
@cookie = REPLACE_WITH_say_session_cookie
@problemId = 1
@threadId = 1
@replyId = 1

### Login redirect (open URL in browser rather than REST Client)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/codeforces/login

### Confirm Codeforces-authenticated SAY session
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/session
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Request CSRF token (required for cookie-authenticated POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE)
# @name csrf
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### SAY account information (no password/email)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Codeforces verified link
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/codeforces/account
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Codeforces contest rating, cached from verified ID token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/codeforces-rating
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Refresh current Codeforces contest rating using public user.info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/codeforces-rating?refresh=true
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Verify a password login is rejected
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"sid_test","password":"wrong"}

### Synchronize current authenticated CF account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/codeforces/sync
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"full":false}

### Poll sync status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/codeforces/sync
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Problem history - choose a real canonical problem_id from here
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/progress?limit=10
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### User skill estimates
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/mastery
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### SAY profile, independent of Codeforces
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/say-profile
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Update SAY display name and bio
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/me/say-profile
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"display_name":"SAY Learner","bio":"Learning greedy and DP"}

### List problem forum threads (set a real CODEFORCES problem_id above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/problems/{{problemId}}/forum/threads?limit=20
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Create a problem thread
# @name createThread
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/problems/{{problemId}}/forum/threads
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"How can I approach this problem?","body":"I tried sorting first. Is that the right direction?","spoiler":false}

### Read a created thread using named response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/forum/threads/{{createThread.response.body.$.thread.id}}
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Create a reply
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forum/threads/{{createThread.response.body.$.thread.id}}/replies
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"body":"Try identifying the greedy invariant.","spoiler":true}

### View replies, reveal spoilers deliberately
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/forum/threads/{{createThread.response.body.$.thread.id}}/replies?reveal_spoilers=true
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}

### Upvote a thread
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/forum/threads/{{createThread.response.body.$.thread.id}}/vote
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"value":1}

### Avatar upload example (REST Client supports multipart include from local file)
# Put an avatar.png in the same directory as this .http file before sending.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/me/avatar
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=RESTClientBoundary

--RESTClientBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="avatar.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./avatar.png
--RESTClientBoundary--

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Cookie: say_session={{cookie}}
X-SAY-CSRF: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
